+| `apps` | `OK apps` followed by one app name per line, in carousel order |
+| `current` | `OK current` followed by `selected=`, `index=`, `mode=` (`home`, `page`, `external`, `home_pending`) and `foreground=` lines |
+| `launch <name>` | `OK launch <resolved name>`; the request is queued and served by the UI thread. Names match case-insensitively, exact first, then a unique prefix. Errors: `ERR unknown app`, `ERR ambiguous app name` |
+| `home` | `OK home` (or `OK home already`); a built-in page returns home, an external app gets SIGTERM to its process group (SIGKILL after 3 s), the same as an ESC long-press |
